</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>FlashOmni Attention</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the generation of sparse symbols <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective of FlashOmni is to implement a general attention kernel that can interpret these symbols and execute arbitrary sparse computations efficiently. In the conventional FlashAttention framework, each CTA processes a complete computation tile. To support sparsity, we extend this design so that each CTA can detect and adapt to different sparsity patterns, as outlined in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 3.3 FlashOmni Sparse Symbols ‣ 3 Method ‣ FlashOmni: A Unified Sparse Attention Engine for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Specifically, before loading <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, each CTA invokes the spatial<span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>axis decoding function <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> (Line 5) and checks <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to determine whether the current tile requires computation. Depending on this result, execution follows either a compute<span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>on<span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>demand or a cache<span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>then<span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>reuse path. The decoding operation uses only bitwise procedures, expressed as <span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text"><math id="S3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{S}_{c},i)=(\mathcal{S}_{c}&gt;&gt;i/n)~\&amp;~1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&gt;&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.274em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.552em">&amp;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{S}_{c},i)=(\mathcal{S}_{c}&gt;&gt;i/n)~\&amp;~1</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the cache<span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>then<span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>reuse path, element<span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>wise computation logic is fused into the FlashOmni attention process, allowing each CTA to choose between standard attention or lightweight element<span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>wise operations (e.g., summation and multiplication in TaylorSeer) based on the decoding result. Alternatively, an elementwise kernel can be invoked to perform simple value-reuse computations and write the results into the output tensor <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding CTA of feature caching can then directly return (Line 7) without further processing. In the compute<span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>on<span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text">-</span>demand path, an additional reduction<span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text">-</span>axis decoding function <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math> (Line 13) is applied before updating <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> in the inner loop to determine whether to skip specific blocks by decoding <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. This operation is defined as <span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text"><math id="S3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}(\mathcal{S}_{s},i,j)=(\mathcal{S}_{s}&gt;&gt;\frac{i}{n}\frac{T_{kv}}{n}+\frac{j}{n})~\&amp;~1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&gt;&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.274em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.552em">&amp;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}(\mathcal{S}_{s},i,j)=(\mathcal{S}_{s}&gt;&gt;\frac{i}{n}\frac{T_{kv}}{n}+\frac{j}{n})~\&amp;~1</annotation></semantics></math></span>. Directly performing this bitwise operation for every <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> load increases CUDA core overhead. To mitigate this, undecoded bits are processed only once when first encountered, and the results—covering up to <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8n</annotation></semantics></math> consecutive blocks—are stored in registers for subsequent reuse.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>FlashOmni Sparse GEMMs</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FlashOmni introduces two <span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">sparse GEMMs</span>, GEMM-<math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and GEMM-<math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>, utilizing <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to remove redundant computations in the Linear layers: query projection (<math id="S3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Proj_{to\_q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><mi>to</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Proj_{to\_q}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and output projection (<math id="S3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Proj_{to\_out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><mi>to</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>out</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Proj_{to\_out}}</annotation></semantics></math>) within attention modules.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Observation 2.</span> In typical attention modules of common DiT architectures, the computation from the input tensor <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> to the final attention output <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> involves three main stages: (1) generating the query vectors <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>; (2) using <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> to compute attention scores with the corresponding keys and aggregating the values; and (3) writing the aggregated results into the output tensor <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, the generation of <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> typically consists of three sequential operations: query projection (<math id="S3.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Proj_{to\_q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><mi>to</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Proj_{to\_q}}</annotation></semantics></math>), token<span id="S3.SS5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>wise RMS normalization (<math id="S3.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{OP_{RMSNorm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>OP</mi><mi>RMSNorm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{OP_{RMSNorm}}</annotation></semantics></math>), and rotary positional encoding (<math id="S3.SS5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{OP_{RoPE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>OP</mi><mi>RoPE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{OP_{RoPE}}</annotation></semantics></math>). The standard attention output formulation <span id="S3.SS5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text"><math id="S3.SS5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{h}_{i}=\sum_{j}P^{h}_{i,j}V^{h}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{h}_{i}=\sum_{j}P^{h}_{i,j}V^{h}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></span> can be expanded as Equation <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.5 FlashOmni Sparse GEMMs ‣ 3 Method ‣ FlashOmni: A Unified Sparse Attention Engine for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{h}_{i}=\sum_{j}\mathrm{Softmax}\left(\frac{\mathrm{OP_{RoPE}}\left(\mathrm{OP_{RMSNorm}}\left(X_{i}W^{h}_{to\_q}\right)\right)(K^{h})^{T}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)_{j}V^{h}_{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>OP</mi><mi>RoPE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>OP</mi><mi>RMSNorm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{h}_{i}=\sum_{j}\mathrm{Softmax}\left(\frac{\mathrm{OP_{RoPE}}\left(\mathrm{OP_{RMSNorm}}\left(X_{i}W^{h}_{to\_q}\right)\right)(K^{h})^{T}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)_{j}V^{h}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Both RMSNorm and RoPE operate exclusively along the feature dimension for each token, without cross<span id="S3.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>token computation. Therefore, at the <span id="S3.SS5.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dispatch</span> step, if <math id="S3.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> specifies that a particular block <math id="S3.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{h}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{h}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is retrieved from the cache <math id="S3.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding query projection <math id="S3.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{h}_{i}=X_{i}W^{h}_{to\_q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{h}_{i}=X_{i}W^{h}_{to\_q}</annotation></semantics></math> can be skipped.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">FlashOmni GEMM-<math id="S3.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math></span>. As shown in the left part of Figure <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3.1 Preliminary ‣ 3 Method ‣ FlashOmni: A Unified Sparse Attention Engine for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> (FlashOmni GEMM-<math id="S3.SS5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>), newly computed <math id="S3.SS5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> values are required to refresh the symbol information at the <span id="S3.SS5.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Update</span> step, and the GEMM-<math id="S3.SS5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> operation will follow its full-standard execution. At the <span id="S3.SS5.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dispatch</span> step, each CTA applies the spatial<span id="S3.SS5.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>axis decoding function <math id="S3.SS5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to determine whether its block tile participates in the upcoming attention computation. If not, the CTA exits immediately without performing any further operations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Observation 3.</span> In typical DiT architectures, once the attention output for each head, <math id="S3.SS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{h}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{h}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, is obtained, an output projection (<math id="S3.SS5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Proj_{to\_out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><mi>to</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>out</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Proj_{to\_out}}</annotation></semantics></math>) is usually applied to facilitate information exchange across heads for the same token, which can be expressed as Equation <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.5 FlashOmni Sparse GEMMs ‣ 3 Method ‣ FlashOmni: A Unified Sparse Attention Engine for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, where the set <math id="S3.SS5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}=\{h\mid J(\mathcal{S}_{c},i,h)=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}=\{h\mid J(\mathcal{S}_{c},i,h)=1\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the heads whose attention outputs are generated directly by attention computation at the current step, rather than obtained via feature caching.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Out_{i}=\sum_{h}O^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}=(\sum_{h\notin H_{i}}+\sum_{h\in H_{i}})O^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Out_{i}=\sum_{h}O^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}=(\sum_{h\notin H_{i}}+\sum_{h\in H_{i}})O^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p">At the <span id="S3.SS5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dispatch</span> step, when <math id="S3.SS5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> specifies that the output features of head <math id="S3.SS5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> for block <math id="S3.SS5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> are retrieved from cache <math id="S3.SS5.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the operation can be expressed as <math id="S3.SS5.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{h}_{i}=\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}(\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>OP</mi><mi>reuse</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{h}_{i}=\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}(\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS5.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\notin H_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\notin H_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.SS5.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>OP</mi><mi>reuse</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an element<span id="S3.SS5.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>wise operation, the following property holds:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{h\notin H_{i}}O^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{h\notin H_{i}}O^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{h\notin H_{i}}\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}(\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i})W_{to\_out}^{h}=\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}(\sum_{h\notin H_{i}}\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>OP</mi><mi>reuse</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>OP</mi><mi>reuse</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{h\notin H_{i}}\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}(\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i})W_{to\_out}^{h}=\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}(\sum_{h\notin H_{i}}\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p10.1" class="ltx_p">This property enables caching of <math id="S3.SS5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h\notin H_{i}}\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h\notin H_{i}}\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> as a bias term <math id="S3.SS5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> at the <span id="S3.SS5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Update</span> step. At later <span id="S3.SS5.p10.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dispatch</span> steps, the cached bias can be transformed using an element<span id="S3.SS5.p10.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>wise kernel, <math id="S3.SS5.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}(\mathcal{B}_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>OP</mi><mi>reuse</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}(\mathcal{B}_{c})</annotation></semantics></math>, and added directly to remaining computations of <math id="S3.SS5.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Proj_{to\_out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><mi>to</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>out</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Proj_{to\_out}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="S3.SS5.p10.1.4" class="ltx_text"><math id="S3.SS5.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h\in H_{i}}O^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h\in H_{i}}O^{h}_{i}W_{to\_out}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></span>) as a bias. This design eliminates redundant reduction<span id="S3.SS5.p10.1.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>axis computations in the GEMM kernel. Furthermore, storing the cache bias removes the need to retain <math id="S3.SS5.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}^{h}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in HBM at <span id="S3.SS5.p10.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Update</span> steps. The related element<span id="S3.SS5.p10.1.7" class="ltx_text">-</span>wise operations in FlashOmni Attention can also be skipped entirely, allowing the cache<span id="S3.SS5.p10.1.8" class="ltx_text">-</span>then<span id="S3.SS5.p10.1.9" class="ltx_text">-</span>reuse branch to terminate immediately. This design reduces both computational cost and memory consumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">FlashOmni GEMM-<math id="S3.SS5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math></span>. As illustrated in the right part of Figure <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3.1 Preliminary ‣ 3 Method ‣ FlashOmni: A Unified Sparse Attention Engine for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> (FlashOmni GEMM-<math id="S3.SS5.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>), the GEMM-<math id="S3.SS5.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> computation is divided into two stages. For each block tile <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{h}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{h}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> along the reduction axis, each CTA applies the reduction-axis decoding function <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to determine whether the tile should be generated via cache<span id="S3.SS5.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>and<span id="S3.SS5.p11.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>reuse or computed on demand. At the <span id="S3.SS5.p11.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Update</span> step, the latest <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and attention outputs <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> are generated, and the cache bias <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is subsequently refreshed. In the first stage, CTAs identify tiles that will be reused at the <span id="S3.SS5.p11.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dispatch</span> step, compute their outputs, and record the results in <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. The second stage then relaunches the kernel, processing the remaining tiles that are always updated through attention computations at the next future steps and adding the cached bias. At the <span id="S3.SS5.p11.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dispatch</span> step, the GEMM-<math id="S3.SS5.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> output space is initialized via <math id="S3.SS5.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>OP</mi><mi>reuse</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{OP_{reuse}}</annotation></semantics></math>, executing only the computations corresponding to the second stage of the <span id="S3.SS5.p11.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Update</span> step. This strategy eliminates redundant operations on cached tiles, thereby reducing both computational workload and memory usage.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Setup</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Models</span>. Our experiments are performed on three SOTA visual generative models: the text<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>to<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>image generator FLUX.1<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>dev <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Black-Forest-Labs, 2024</a>)</cite>, the text<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>to<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text">-</span>video generator HunyuanVideo <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kong et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and the text<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text">-</span>guided image editing model FLUX.1<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text">-</span>Kontext <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Batifol et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Benchmarks and Metrics</span>.
For the text<span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>to<span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>image generation experiments, we conduct inference on the COCO<span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>2017 dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al., 2014</a>)</cite> at a resolution of <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024\times 1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024\times 1024</annotation></semantics></math> pixels. The text<span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>guided image editing evaluation is performed on KontextBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Batifol et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which contains 1,026 unique image–prompt pairs derived from 108 base images. Generated outputs are assessed using CLIP<span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text">-</span>IQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and FID<span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text">-</span>FP16 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Heusel et al., 2017</a>)</cite>, measuring image quality and distributional similarity, respectively. For text<span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text">-</span>to<span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text">-</span>video generation, we adopt VBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> to evaluate various aspects of video quality, including background consistency, motion smoothness, temporal flicker, and stylistic coherence. Fidelity to the original results is quantified using PSNR, SSIM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2004</a>)</cite>, and LPIPS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2018</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To measure computational efficiency of sparse attention, we report TOPS (tera<span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>operations per second), defined as <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{attn}/\texttt{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">attn</mtext><mo>/</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">t</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{attn}/\texttt{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sparsity</span>, defined as (<span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">skip</span> / <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">total</span>) following SpargeAttn <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>. Here, <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">attn</span> denotes the total number of operations in a standard attention computation, <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">t</span> is the latency from given <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q,K,V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q,K,V)</annotation></semantics></math> inputs to the corresponding attention outputs, <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">skip</span> is the number of skipped attention pairs <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q_{i}K_{j}^{\top},\widetilde{P}_{ij}V_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q_{i}K_{j}^{\top},\widetilde{P}_{ij}V_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">total</span> is the total number of such pairs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines and Platform</span>. We compare FlashOmni with five SOTA baselines: two block<span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>sparse attention skipping methods: SpargeAttn <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite> and DiTFastAttnV2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>, and three feature caching methods: ToCa <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zou et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, FORA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Selvaraju et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and TaylorSeer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>. The configuration for FlashOmni is specified as <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau_{q},\tau_{kv},\mathcal{N},\mathcal{D},S_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau_{q},\tau_{kv},\mathcal{N},\mathcal{D},S_{q})</annotation></semantics></math> (Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1.SSS1" title="A.1.1 Setup ‣ A.1 Experimental Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ FlashOmni: A Unified Sparse Attention Engine for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1.1</span></a>). All experiments are executed on a single NVIDIA A100 GPU.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>
End-to-end metrics comparison with block-sparse skipping across image and video generation models.
</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S4.T1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:80.4pt;vertical-align:-38.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-131.8pt,26.6pt) scale(0.6013329309608,0.6013329309608) ;">
<table id="S4.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span>(seq_len)</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Configuration</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TOPS (<math id="S4.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sparsity (%, <math id="S4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PSNR (<math id="S4.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LPIPS (<math id="S4.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SSIM <math id="S4.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CLIP-IQA (<math id="S4.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
