<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Experimental Details</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.1 </span>Setup</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As is metioned in 4.1, the configuration for FlashOmni is specified as <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau_{q},\tau_{kv},\mathcal{N},\mathcal{D},S_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau_{q},\tau_{kv},\mathcal{N},\mathcal{D},S_{q})</annotation></semantics></math>. In Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.1.1 Setup ‣ A.1 Experimental Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ FlashOmni: A Unified Sparse Attention Engine for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we give details about them.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Settings</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A1.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Description</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.T4.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-1.5pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{q}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:227.6pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Sparsity threshold for <math id="A1.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.
Details: the importance scores of tokens are sorted in ascending order, and
tokens are progressively marked for sparsification until the cumulative importance
of the selected tokens exceeds <math id="A1.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.T4.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-1.5pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:227.6pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Sparsity threshold for kv. Details: the importance scores of blocks are sorted in ascending order, and blocks are progressively marked for sparsification until the cumulative importance of the selected blocks exceeds <math id="A1.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:227.6pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Moderate cache interval.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:227.6pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Order of expansion.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.T4.2.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.7pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{q}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:227.6pt;">
<span id="A1.T4.2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Threshold of caching. Details: if the proportion of tokens requiring computation is below this threshold, the layer degenerates into feature caching.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Settings and their descriptions.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is worth noting that the values of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math> are not set to their target values at the initial time step. Rather, they progressively converge to these values as the time step advances.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We conducted experiments on three models for different tasks: FLUX for the text-to-image generator, HunyuanVideo for the text-to-video generator, and FLUX.1-Kontext for text-guided image editing. We selected five representative parameters for evaluation, including <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> at 5% and 50%; <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math> at 15%, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> of 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7; <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> of 0, 1, and 2; <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> at 0% and 30%. Our experiments achieved excellent results, maintaining high generation quality even under high sparsity levels. It is worth noting that these parameters can be efficiently tuned via lightweight search algorithms to further enhance the performance of FlashOmni. We plan to implement this optimization in future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.2 </span>GEMM-<math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> Speedup Metrics</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we define our methodology for computing the speedup metric of GEMM-<math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{total}</annotation></semantics></math> as the total time taken to execute a single <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Proj_{to\_out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mrow><mi>to</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>out</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Proj_{to\_out}}</annotation></semantics></math> operation and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the sparsity ratio, then we can compute the normal time consumption: <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}T_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}T_{total}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the FlashOmni time consumption:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\text{FlashOmini}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>FlashOmini</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\text{FlashOmini}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T_{\text{sparse}}+T_{\text{computation}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>sparse</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>computation</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T_{\text{sparse}}+T_{\text{computation}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T_{\text{total}}\times s+\sum_{\mathcal{N}}\left((1-s)\times T_{\text{total}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T_{\text{total}}\times s+\sum_{\mathcal{N}}\left((1-s)\times T_{\text{total}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T_{\text{total}}+(\mathcal{N}-1)(1-s)T_{\text{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T_{\text{total}}+(\mathcal{N}-1)(1-s)T_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then we can compute the speedup metric <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathcal{N}}{1+(\mathcal{N}-1)(1-s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathcal{N}}{1+(\mathcal{N}-1)(1-s)}</annotation></semantics></math>. When the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=0.9</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}=6</annotation></semantics></math>, the theoretical speedup is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{6}{1+(6-1)(1-0.9)}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{6}{1+(6-1)(1-0.9)}=4</annotation></semantics></math>. As is shown in Figure <a href="#S4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 4.3 Efficiency Evaluation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ FlashOmni: A Unified Sparse Attention Engine for Diffusion Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, our actual speedup obtained under this configuration is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3.509\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.509</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.509\times</annotation></semantics></math>, approaching the theoretical value of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times</annotation></semantics></math>, which substantiates the high efficiency of FlashOmni.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.3 </span>Warmup Steps Analysis for FLUX</h4>

<figure id="A1.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.25401v1/ablation_warmup.svg" id="A1.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/220;" width="548" height="220"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>End-to-end metrics comparison with feature caching on FLUX with different warmup steps.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.T5" class="ltx_table ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center">
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<div id="A1.T5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:318.0pt;height:71.7pt;vertical-align:-34.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-58.3pt,13.1pt) scale(0.731770985129133,0.731770985129133) ;">
<table id="A1.T5.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T5.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T5.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></td>
<td id="A1.T5.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="A1.T5.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Configuration</span></td>
<td id="A1.T5.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="A1.T5.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PSNR (<math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="A1.T5.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="A1.T5.1.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LPIPS (<math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="A1.T5.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="A1.T5.1.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SSIM <math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A1.T5.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="A1.T5.1.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FID (<math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r"><span id="A1.T5.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FLUX.1-Kontext</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Full-Attention</td>
<td id="A1.T5.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">50 steps</td>
<td id="A1.T5.1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
